{"name":"Tobermory","hex":"#d39898","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tobermory","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village, the main settlement on the island of Mull in Argyll and Bute council area, Scotland .","A community in Northern Bruce Peninsula municipality, Bruce County, Ontario, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tobermory"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tobermory, Mull","blocks":[{"text":"Tobermory is a harbour town in the Inner Hebrides, Scotland. It is the main town and capital of the Isle of Mull, approximately 120 miles northwest of Edinburgh, 76 miles northwest of Glasgow, and 91 miles west-southwest of Inverness. It had a population of 1,045 in 2022."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Tobermory_waterfront_recrop.jpg/330px-Tobermory_waterfront_recrop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tobermory%2C_Mull"},{"title":"Tobermory distillery","blocks":[{"text":"Tobermory distillery is an Island single malt Scotch whisky and gin distillery located on the Hebridean island of Mull, Scotland in the town of Tobermory"}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Tobermory_Distillery_%2846047208591%29.jpg/330px-Tobermory_Distillery_%2846047208591%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tobermory_distillery"},{"title":"Tobermory (short story)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Tobermory\" is a humorous short story by Hector Hugh Munro written under his pen-name, Saki. It was originally published in The Westminster Gazette in 1909, first collected, in a revised form, in The Chronicles of Clovis (1911), and has frequently been reprinted in anthologies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/H%C3%A9ctor_Hugh_Munro.png/330px-H%C3%A9ctor_Hugh_Munro.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=a